\section{Example I: Knox cube test data}

This example uses the classic Knox Cube test data \cite{wright-stone}. The Knox Cube Test measures short term memory and consists of 18 dichotomous items. In the data set responses from 35 subjects were considered. For four items all respondents gave the same answer and these items are not considered in what follows. Item fit statistics for the remaining 14 items are shown in Table \ref{knox} below.

