\section{Example III: Simulation study}
The simulated data sets used $k$ polytomous items simulated from

The person locations were simulated from a normal distribution with mean $\mu$ and SD 1. All combinations of the four conditions: (a) number of items ($k=10,15,20$); (b) number of persons ($N=100,200,300,400,500,600,700,800,900,1000$); (c) mean value in the distribution of the latent variable ($\mu=0,2$) were simulated. This yielded a total of 60 different setups, and for each of these we simulated 10000 data sets in order to find the empirical percentiles of the null distribution of the item fit statistics.

